      "Before safe/non-null entry, convert nullable/undefined foreign values through the declared Option/Result, checked-wrapper or opaque-foreign-value contract; declared nullable Option absence may produce None without inventing an error. Separately translate foreign/host error returns, errno-like state, exceptions, panics, rejected promises, signals and exit statuses into declared typed Gravity error contracts. Do not convert a real error or capability denial into absence. Retain host/foreign type identity, ownership transfer on failure, cleanup, abort policy, runtime dependencies and exception/null contracts for hosted dispatch.",
