     "a1fa8f9d63041a88e3789d8f65696986d76281a887188b03a65e63448479987f",
     :raw
     "For operands with applicable Gravity binary value equality, `(not= left right)`\nreturns the Bool complement of `(= left right)`. Both operands follow ordinary\nL2 evaluation left to right, exactly once; their effects are preserved, and a\ncontrol transfer aborts invocation. Inequality does not introduce an equality\ndomain, coercion, identity comparison or variadic rule, nor does it evaluate\nstored payloads beyond the applicable equality contract. `gravity.core` owns\nthis operation; numeric, collection, profile, target, effect, capability and\nsafety requirements remain with their governing contracts.\n"}
    {:facet
     {:id "stdlib/facet/std2/4216-4871",
      :document-id "STD2",
      :source-occurrence-id
      "STD2/source/ecf36f320e1baba20c84867f482a9bfb766d1946f26215b78a164c37678bd4e3",
      :kind :acceptance-rule,
      :start-byte 4216,
      :end-byte 4871,
      :raw-sha256
      "7f7deae6c9d34be5f94d533bbe70be225c09a0c3f1d6cdd697279a7cf0774661"},
     :path
     "docs/phase-16-standard-library/212-std2-core-library-specification.md",
     :ref "86747916c4c876d707a1548113409fb939d854c9",
     :file-sha256
     "a1fa8f9d63041a88e3789d8f65696986d76281a887188b03a65e63448479987f",
     :raw
     "Unary `(nil? value)` returns Bool true exactly when the normally evaluated\nvalue is nil, and false for other normally evaluated values. False and empty\ncollections are not implicitly nil; the query does not unwrap Option or Result\nvalues. Its operand follows ordinary L2 evaluation exactly once; operand\neffects are preserved, and a control transfer aborts invocation. The query\ndoes not evaluate stored payloads, mutate the value or itself construct a\ncollection. `gravity.core` owns this predicate. Flow-typing and representation\npolicies are not selected here; existing profile, target, effect, capability\nand safety legality requirements still apply.\n"}
    {:facet
     {:id "stdlib/facet/std2/4901-5557",
